; Direct ink writing of a layered bar, 45 x 4 x 2.905 mm, layers stacked along z
; Design with alumina layers of 70 um and PMMA interlayers of 35 um
; Parameters as name, value, unit and source
;   nozzle_diameter_um 250 um (assumption: design)
;   max_layer_height_fraction 0.8 nozzle diameters (assumption: design)
;   min_layer_height_fraction 0.3 nozzle diameters (assumption: design)
;   print_speed_mm_s 10 mm/s (assumption: design)
;   travel_speed_mm_s 30 mm/s (assumption: design)
;   syringe_diameter_mm 14.5 mm (assumption: design)
;   z_hop_mm 1 mm (assumption: design)
;   tool_change_s 30 s (assumption: design)
; Layer plan
;   28 alumina layers of 70 um, each in 1 pass of 70 um, tool T0
;   27 PMMA interlayers of 35 um, each in 1 pass of 35 um, tool T1
;   55 passes, serpentine raster with road spacing 250 um, 0 and 90 degrees alternating
; Origin at a corner of the bar footprint on the build plate. XYZ absolute in mm, Z at the top of each pass.
; E is syringe plunger travel in mm, road width x pass height x road length over the plunger area of 165.13 mm^2.
; T0 holds the alumina paste and T1 the PMMA paste. The tool offsets are set in the printer firmware.
; A 70 um alumina pass is thinner than the 75 um smallest pass of a 250 um nozzle, so this film is better made by dip or spray coating.
; A 35 um PMMA pass is thinner than the 75 um smallest pass of a 250 um nozzle, so this film is better made by dip or spray coating.
; Estimated print time 93.8 min
;
G21 ; mm
G90 ; absolute XYZ
M83 ; relative E
G28 ; home
